<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103634" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεττῑγο-φόρας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wearing a</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέττιξ</span>, as the Athenians were
			called, because in early times <i>they wore golden</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέττιγες</span>, as a token that they were
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτόχθονες</span> (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέττιξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.2
				</span></i>
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεττιγομήτρα</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1331
			</span></i> (anap.): also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεττῑγο-φόρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				395.34
			</span></i>: hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεττῑγο-φορία</span></b> , ἡ, <i><span class="en">
				Tz.
				<u>H.</u>
				1.233
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
